\section*{Universal Bounds on Atomic Excess Charge}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. Coulomb molecules are claimed to bind at most $Z+CM$ electrons, and neutral atoms to have universally bounded first ionization energy and half-electron exterior radius.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Ground states are compared across particle sectors using common localization and screening fields. Local count bounds, changes of observation law, and estimates in nuclear voids control excess particles; deterministic comparison fields give both sides of the neutral-atom energy and radius bounds.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The universal excess-charge theorem gives n<=Z+CM under strict binding for all Coulomb molecules, with a position- and charge-independent constant. Taking one nucleus M=1 gives the full atomic Z+C target; molecules and every real Z>=1 extend it. The claimed conclusion supplies the requested case and extends it in the directions just specified.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 263, the documented entries give the large-$m$ ionization-energy coefficient and the generalized neutral outer-radius asymptotics. Fixed-$m$ limits and the general uniform excess-charge manuscript are not selected. No Comparator is assigned to the selected manuscript here; the family page selects other papers or supporting statements. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{Uniform excess charge for Coulomb molecules and the outer radius of neutral atoms}, 2026-09-24; citation key \texttt{OAI:Uniform-excess-charge-for-Coulomb-molecules-and-the-outer-radius-of-neutral-atoms-September-24-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Uniform-excess-charge-for-Coulomb-molecules-and-the-outer-radius-of-neutral-atoms-September-24-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Uniform-excess-charge-for-Coulomb-molecules-and-the-outer-radius-of-neutral-atoms-September-24-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Uniform-excess-charge-for-Coulomb-molecules-and-the-outer-radius-of-neutral-atoms-September-24-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/Uniform-excess-charge-for-Coulomb-molecules-and-the-outer-radius-of-neutral-atoms-September-24-2026/paper.pdf}{Latest version}.
\item Family 263: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/docs/263.md}{Lean scope}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/CONTENTS.md}{OpenAI catalogue entry}.
\end{itemize}
\end{document}

